I've encountered very strange behaviour of shopkeepers. 
Normally a shopkeeper avoids traps. However when one has stolen
something out of a shop, and the shopkeeper decides to follow you
He will pass traps which are between him and the door (e.g. 
before the door opening, inside the shop) This looks like a bug
to me (I'd like to have him delayed by pits I dig in the door 
opening!).

Also I don't think its fair that the shopkeeper immediately
knows where to find you whenever you teleport away from a shop.
He/she should at least have some trouble locating me.
Oh well, maybe shopkeepers possess some supranatural senses.

